load @term/seed/code/type/term
  find term

# The automatic verification layer, refinement types backed by decision procedures. A refinement type is a base type
# carved down by a predicate, the integers that are non-negative, the index that is below the array length, so the type
# itself records a proof obligation. Where the obligation falls in a decidable fragment (linear arithmetic, the
# commutative-ring identities, the quadratic sum-of-squares inequalities, modular bounds), it is discharged
# automatically by the prover with no proof written by hand, the way Dafny, Liquid Haskell, and F-star do it. What the
# automatic deciders cannot close is handed down to the kernel as an explicit proof obligation. This layer is why most
# proofs in the library are free: the universal ring identities, the order laws, and the inequalities are all
# discharged here. The form carries the refined term; the predicate and its automatic discharge are the mechanism.
form refinement-type
  link term, like term
